{
  "abstract": "Exactly eleven positive nonprimes n satisfy gcd(d²−1,n)>1 for every proper positive divisor d of n. Exactly four of them, 6, 30, 42 and 1722, are midpoints of twin primes. We prove completeness by descent on the largest prime factor and verify the resulting finite tree in Lean.",
